{"slug":"ops-prod-ops","title":"Production operations","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Production hosts (canonical)"},{"id":"b2","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Fact"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Value"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Content instance"}],[{"type":"text","value":"guerrilla "},{"type":"text","value":"157.180.90.121","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", https://guerrilla.barkpark.cloud; "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy/instance-deploy.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on merge"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Control plane"}],[{"type":"text","value":"barkpark-cp "},{"type":"text","value":"178.105.92.191","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", https://barkpark.cloud; "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy/cp-deploy.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (Docker Compose slots)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Retired"}],[{"type":"text","value":"barkpark-cms "},{"type":"text","value":"89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", the pull-deployed box, deleted 2026-10-03 (snapshot 439115764). Docs calling it prod are history."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"App dir (guerrilla)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", one checkout, per-slot build roots "},{"type":"text","value":"api/_build_blue","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"_build_green","marks":["code"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Service"}],[{"type":"text","value":"systemd "},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark-slot@blue","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (:4000) / "},{"type":"text","value":"@green","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (:4001), one live at a time; "},{"type":"text","value":"ExecStart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (ASDF + "},{"type":"text","value":".env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Proxy"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Caddy; the "},{"type":"text","value":"/etc/caddy/Caddyfile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" upstream names the live slot — read it; smoke by the PUBLIC URL"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Erlang/Elixir"}],[{"type":"text","value":"ASDF, pinned by repo-root "},{"type":"text","value":".tool-versions","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"text","value":"erlang 27.3.4","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"elixir 1.18.4-otp-27","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (Past Mistake #6)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Env file"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark/.env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"DATABASE_URL","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"SECRET_KEY_BASE","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_EXTRA_ORIGINS","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ws origins) + "},{"type":"text","value":".slots/<slot>.env","marks":["code"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Logs"}],[{"type":"text","value":"U='-u barkpark -u barkpark-slot@blue -u barkpark-slot@green'; journalctl $U -f","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — all three; which exists varies. "},{"type":"text","value":"-- No entries --","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" = \"could not look\", not \"none\": re-run unfiltered, quote the total."}]]]},{"id":"b3","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Pipeline, routing and slot flips: "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy/README.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Golden Rules 2/3/6 apply."}]},{"id":"b4","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The toolchain pin is a production change.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" A box's asdf reads repo-root "},{"type":"text","value":".tool-versions","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", so editing it moves prod — never in a PR touching anything else. "},{"type":"text","value":"elixir.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" carries the same 1.18.4 (green prod-compile = \"compiles on the box\") and pins "},{"type":"text","value":"otp: \"27.0\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" below the box's 27.3.4 on purpose: wider blast radius."}]},{"id":"b5","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The postcheck rule"},{"id":"b6","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A misbooted or stopped node looks identical to a healthy one from outside — systemd returned, SSH closed, nothing surfaced. So any workflow touching "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on prod "},{"type":"text","value":"must","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" end with "},{"type":"text","value":"api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", which probes the public HTTP surface."}]},{"id":"b7","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Atomic transitions:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" prefer "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to stop-then-start (document a deliberate stop), and a Makefile target to ad-hoc "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"No silent ops:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" SSH'd in to patch something? Run the script before you log out; refuse \"looks fine, didn't check.\""}]]},{"id":"b8","type":"code","value":"ssh root@<prod-host> \"cd /opt/barkpark && ./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh\"\n# QUOTED, or the cd runs on your laptop. On the box: drop the ssh."},{"id":"b9","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"It runs "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl is-active --quiet barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", STARTING an inactive service — a guardrail, not a monitor: run it only when \"should be running\" is the desired end state; sleeps 2 s for the BEAM to bind its port; then requires HTTP 200 from "},{"type":"text","value":"/api/schemas","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (unauth JSON — swap to "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" if retired, never admin-gated "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/schemas/production","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Exit 0 = "},{"type":"text","value":"PASS prod healthy …","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; non-zero writes a "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" tail to stderr — read it, then "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl $U -n 200 --no-pager","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"$U","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" above), never retry blindly. After a deploy also tail "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl $U -f","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" >=60 s for boot errors, restart loops, 5xx controllers."}]},{"id":"b10","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Operator one-shots"},{"id":"b11","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"barkpark.edges.backfill","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (and "},{"type":"text","value":"media.backfill","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"paper.backfill_block_ids","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"paper.composition_migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") boot a NARROWED tree ("},{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark.OneShot","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") — no Endpoint, so an inherited "},{"type":"text","value":"PHX_SERVER","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" cannot bind the live slot's port, as on guerrilla 2026-09-02 (\"port 4001 already in use\"). Mix still COMPILES. ON THE BOX, in "},{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"id":"b12","type":"code","value":"slot=$(systemctl is-active --quiet barkpark-slot@green && echo green || echo blue)\nset -a; . ./.env; . ./.slots/$slot.env; set +a  # unit env; sets MIX_BUILD_ROOT\ncd api && MIX_ENV=prod nice -n 19 mix barkpark.edges.backfill  # dry run"},{"id":"b13","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"MIX_BUILD_ROOT","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" must be the ACTIVE slot's warm root with the checkout at its sha, or mix recompiles under the serving BEAM; "},{"type":"text","value":"nice","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — that boot took the 2-core box from load 1.9 to 6.3. No "},{"type":"text","value":".slots/","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"text","value":". ./.env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" alone, default "},{"type":"text","value":"_build","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Bare = dry run, "},{"type":"text","value":"--apply","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" writes."}]},{"id":"b14","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Prod migrations"},{"id":"b15","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"instance-deploy.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" runs "},{"type":"text","value":"ecto.migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" from the idle slot's new build while the live slot serves, and on failure exits 13 without a flip (checkout reset). The control plane migrates when its idle Compose slot boots. Old and new code share the new schema during the swap, so migrations must be expand/contract. Destructive migrations (drop/rename) have no zero-downtime order — schedule a window. Never "},{"type":"text","value":"make reset-db","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"mix ecto.reset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on prod; a mid-way failure gets a forward fix, never an edit to an applied one."}]},{"id":"b16","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Rollback"},{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Roll back by reverting source ("},{"type":"text","value":"git revert <bad-sha>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", as a PR); its merge redeploys through "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". For an immediate flip back, both scripts carry "},{"type":"text","value":"--rollback","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"instance-deploy.sh --rollback-preflight","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" first). Never "},{"type":"text","value":"git reset --hard","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or force-push a prod checkout by hand, and never hand-roll a partial clean, which serves stale BEAM/HEEx (Past Mistakes #1-3). Reverting code does NOT undo a schema change; write a compensating migration."}]},{"id":"b18","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Code anchors"},{"id":"b19","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the postcheck"}],[{"type":"text","value":"deploy/instance-deploy.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — content-instance deploy, migrate, flip, rollback"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Makefile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":"rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (single-checkout boxes)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — systemd wrapper (ASDF + "},{"type":"text","value":".env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]]}],"related":["ops-npm-rollback-playbook"]}
